    {
      "layer": "economic_commercial",
      "tag": "resource_concentration",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "The Rammelsberg silver mines in the Harz mountains gave Saxon dukes a continuous revenue stream independent of royal grants, funding the Ottonian dynasty's military campaigns and church construction.",
